  "slug": "functions-augmenting-0a1b",
  "summary": "Several preprints build learned or empirical mappings from N-body halos to galaxies, tSZ maps and mass maps, aimed at survey-scale forward modelling.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is constructing observables on top of dark-matter-only simulations or recovering underlying matter and gas fields from data. On the forward side, Extremely Randomized Trees and Gaussian Processes populate the 2.8 Gpc FLAMINGO-10k DMO run with a galaxy catalogue. Baryonification V derives thermal SZ Compton-y maps from DMO light cones. An empirical model predicts individual halo concentrations from assembly histories in CDM and WDM over z=0–5. A flexible halo–stellar mass–SFR–UV model is fit to JWST luminosity functions and angular correlations at z>6. Inverse problems use deep learning trained on simulations. One CNN recovers cluster mass maps and subhalos from HST imaging, consistent with CLASH lensing. Another reconstructs IGM column densities from KCWI Lyα cubes of z~2.3 protoclusters. The LSST DESC cluster pipeline, validated on cosmoDC2, illustrates the survey-level consumer of such models, constraining Ω_c and σ_8.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
